---
/**
 * TEACHING PHILOSOPHY — how Sunbeam believes teaching should happen.
 *
 * ═══ SOURCE OF TRUTH ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 *
 * Fetched from the school's own site. Every claim below traces to one of these
 * sentences, and where the school's wording carries the idea better than a
 * rewrite would, it is quoted rather than paraphrased:
 *
 *   /principals-message/
 *     "all the students do not have the same talents and so each one will
 *      achieve success differently"
 *     "We, educators being as a facilitators should always encourage our child
 *      to develop in their specific field of interest"
 *     "incorporate such activities that help the all-round development of each
 *      child"
 *
 *   /about-us/
 *     "Incorporate Technology, a theory of Multiple Intelligence and
 *      Collaborative learning in all areas of teaching."
 *     "Develop in children a degree of independence and self-motivation."
 *     "Provide all children with a secure, caring, friendly and well-organized
 *      environment where discipline is consistent."
 *
 *   /  (Principal Speak)
 *     "education is not merely about imparting knowledge, but about nurturing
 *      character"
 *     "innovative teaching methods meet modern technology"
 *     "Our classrooms are places of curiosity and collaboration"
 *     "every child feels valued, safe, and inspired to achieve their full
 *      potential"
 *
 * ⚠ NOTHING ELSE IS CLAIMED. No pedagogy, framework or method appears here that
 * the school has not published. Three of the brief's ideas — individual
 * potential, independence, collaboration — are NOT in the Principal's Message;
 * they come from About Us, and the attributions below say so rather than
 * crediting the Principal with words she did not write.
 *
 * ═══ SCOPE ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 *
 * ⚠ THIS PAGE STOPS AT TEACHING. Curriculum, experiential and project work,
 * STEM, robotics, AI, smart classrooms, assessment, careers, structure and
 * parent partnership each have their own page, and §05 in particular is written
 * to stay on the PHILOSOPHY of teaching with technology rather than drifting
 * into the rooms and equipment that belong to Smart Classrooms.
 *
 * ⚠ IT USES THE SITE'S OWN MOTION CONTRACT — data-split, data-reveal(+delay),
 * data-pop, data-parallax, data-mask — handled by scripts/motion-gsap.ts, which
 * is already gated on prefers-reduced-motion and Save-Data. No new JS ships.
 */
import SmartImage from '../../components/ui/SmartImage.astro';

/* Photography — verified Ballia frames only. */
/* The constellation's core. A wide ceremony frame was here first and read as
   noise once cropped to a 200px circle — this one holds two faces and a pair of
   working hands at that size, and it is a making intelligence in the middle of a
   diagram about there being more than one. */
/**
 * §02's pair. The section draws a teacher and a learner joined by a connector,
 * so both ends have to actually BE that.
 *
 * ⚠ THE FRAMES THAT WERE HERE FIRST SHOWED NOBODY. §02 used the activity-lab and
 * library shots with alt text reading "a teacher working with a group" and "a
 * student reading in the Nalanda Library" — and both of those files, along with
 * the computer-lab frame, are from an empty-campus shoot: no people, chairs
 * stacked, machines under dust covers. The alt text described a scene that did
 * not exist, which is an invented claim a screen-reader user has no way to
 * check. These two are people actually teaching and actually working.
 */

/* Decorative transparent PNGs — used as ornament, never as bullet glyphs. */
import dBulb from '../../assets/icons/bulb.png';
import dBooks from '../../assets/icons/books.png';
import dRocket from '../../assets/icons/rocketpaper.png';
import dStars from '../../assets/icons/two-stars.png';
import dKite from '../../assets/icons/kite.png';
/* The four the client supplied for this constellation. Named for the nodes
   they belong to, so a future swap is obvious. */
import dShape from '../../assets/icons/shape-2.png';
import { getTeachingPhilosophy } from '../../lib/cms';
import RichLine from '../ui/RichLine.astro';
import { fileUrl } from '../../lib/cms';



/**
 * The constellation for §03. Each node is an ABILITY, and each carries a real
 * asset rather than a drawn icon — the brief's instruction, and the reason the
 * set reads as the school's own rather than as stock.
 */
/**
 * Ring radius as a percentage of the square stage.
 *
 * ⚠ NODES ARE PLACED BY PERCENTAGE, NOT BY A ROTATE→TRANSLATE TRANSFORM. The
 * first build used `transform: rotate(var(--a)) translate(clamp(...))` with a
 * counter-rotation on the inner span. The rule shipped intact — it is in the
 * built CSS — but `transform` computed to `none` on every node, so all seven
 * collapsed onto the centre and sat on top of the learner's portrait. Measured,
 * not assumed: getComputedStyle reported "none" while the child's standalone
 * `rotate`/`translate` in the same file applied fine.
 *
 * Trigonometry at build time sidesteps it entirely: each node gets a plain
 * left/top percentage, which needs no rotation and therefore no counter-rotation
 * to keep the label upright. 36% clears the 19% core and the ~9% node half-width
 * with room either side.
 */
const R = 40;

/* ⚠ FOUR OF THE SEVEN CARRY THE CLIENT’S OWN ICONS; the other three keep the
   ornament set this page was built with. Nothing else about the constellation
   changed — the angles are still evenly spaced and still derived from R. */
const tp = await getTeachingPhilosophy();
const { one, two, three, four, five, close } = tp;

/**
 * ⚠ THE ANGLE IS COMPUTED, NOT STORED. Each node sits at an even share of the
 * circle, so seven cards are 0°, 51°, 103° … — exactly `i × 360 ÷ cards`. It was
 * stored once, per card, which meant an editor could drag a node off the ring or
 * add an eighth that overlapped the first. The ring now re-spaces itself.
 */
const angleOf = (i) => (i * 360) / three.cards.length;
---

<div class="tp">
  {/* ═══ 01 · EVERY CHILD IS DIFFERENT ══════════════════════════════════════
      A single large frame with the statement crossing it, and the number set
      oversized behind the copy — the page's loudest idea, stated once. */}
  <section class="tp-one" aria-labelledby="tp-one-h">
    <span class="tp__grid" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="tp__wash tp__wash--a" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <div class="u-container tp-one__in">
      <div class="tp-one__copy">
        <p class="tp__n" aria-hidden="true">01</p>
        <p class="tp__k t-label" data-reveal>{one.kicker}</p>
        <h2 class="tp-one__h" id="tp-one-h" data-split>
          {one.heading} <em>{one.headingEm}</em>
        </h2>

        {/* ⚠ THE CURLY QUOTES ARE TYPOGRAPHY AND STAY HERE. An editor types the
            sentence; the design puts the marks round it. Storing them means one
            can be deleted and the other left. */}
        <blockquote class="tp-quote" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="110">
          <p>“{one.quote}”</p>
          <cite>{one.quoteAuthor} · Principal</cite>
        </blockquote>

        <RichLine class="tp__p" text={one.body[0]} reveal revealDelay={200} />
      </div>

      <figure class="tp-one__art" data-mask>
        <SmartImage
          file={one.image}
          alt={one.imageAlt}
         
          widths={[520, 900, 1200]}
          sizes="(max-width: 900px) 92vw, 46vw"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      </figure>
    </div>

    <img class="tp__f tp__f--kite" src={dKite.src} alt="" aria-hidden="true" data-parallax data-parallax-y="56" />
    <img class="tp__f tp__f--stars" src={dStars.src} alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
  </section>

  {/* ═══ 02 · TEACHERS AS FACILITATORS ══════════════════════════════════════
      Two frames on a diagonal with a drawn connector between them — the
      teacher→student relationship shown as a relationship, not as two columns. */}
  <section class="tp-two" aria-labelledby="tp-two-h">
    <span class="tp__dots" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <div class="u-container tp-two__in">
      <div class="tp-two__stage">
        <figure class="tp-two__a" data-parallax data-parallax-y="38">
          <SmartImage file={two.imageUpper} alt={two.imageUpperAlt} widths={[420, 780]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 88vw, 30vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        </figure>

        {/* The connector. Drawn, decorative, and the reason this reads as one
            gesture rather than two pictures. */}
        <svg class="tp-two__link" viewBox="0 0 240 160" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M8 22C86 22 150 74 232 138" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="7 9" stroke-linecap="round" />
          <circle cx="8" cy="22" r="5" fill="currentColor" />
          <circle cx="232" cy="138" r="5" fill="currentColor" />
        </svg>

        <figure class="tp-two__b" data-parallax data-parallax-y="-34">
          <SmartImage file={two.imageLower} alt={two.imageLowerAlt} widths={[420, 780]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 74vw, 26vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-two__copy">
        <p class="tp__n" aria-hidden="true">02</p>
        <p class="tp__k t-label" data-reveal>{two.kicker}</p>
        <h2 class="tp-two__h" id="tp-two-h" data-split>{two.heading}</h2>

        <blockquote class="tp-quote" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="110">
          <p>“{two.quote}”</p>
          <cite>{two.quoteAuthor} · Principal</cite>
        </blockquote>

        <RichLine class="tp__p" text={two.body[0]} reveal revealDelay={190} />
      </div>
    </div>

    <img class="tp__f tp__f--bulb" src={dBulb.src} alt="" aria-hidden="true" data-parallax data-parallax-y="-44" />
  </section>

  {/* ═══ 03 · MULTIPLE INTELLIGENCES ════════════════════════════════════════
      A constellation: the learner at the centre, abilities orbiting on real
      assets, joined by drawn rays. Deliberately NOT a grid of icon cards. */}
  <section class="tp-three" aria-labelledby="tp-three-h">
    <span class="tp__orb" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="tp__dots tp__dots--dark" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <div class="u-container tp-three__in">
      <header class="tp-three__head">
        <p class="tp__n tp__n--onink" aria-hidden="true">03</p>
        <p class="tp__k tp__k--onink t-label" data-reveal>{three.kicker}</p>
        <h2 class="tp-three__h" id="tp-three-h" data-split>{three.heading}</h2>
        <RichLine class="tp__p tp__p--onink" text={three.body[0]} reveal revealDelay={110} />
      </header>

      <div class="tp-const" data-reveal>
        <div class="tp-const__core">
          <SmartImage file={three.image} alt={three.imageAlt} widths={[320, 560]} sizes="(max-width: 700px) 46vw, 260px" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        </div>

        {/* ⚠ THE RINGS ARE ONE SVG, NOT SEVEN BORDERED DIVS. Concentric rings
            drawn as elements would each need their own box and would round
            differently at each breakpoint; one viewBox scales exactly. */}
        <svg class="tp-const__rings" viewBox="0 0 400 400" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          {/* r IS DERIVED, NOT CHOSEN. The viewBox is 400 wide, so a percentage of
              the stage is 4× its number: the dashed ring is R (40 → 160) and
              therefore runs exactly through the node centres, and the solid one
              sits at 92, a hair outside the 64-radius core. Hard-coded 128/170
              were here first and matched neither, which is why the nodes looked
              scattered between two unrelated circles rather than placed on one. */}
          <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="92" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" />
          <circle class="tp-const__dash" cx="200" cy="200" r={R * 4} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 10" />
        </svg>

        <ul class="tp-const__set">
          {
            three.cards.map((ab, i) => (
              <li
                class="node"
                style={`--x: ${(50 + R * Math.cos((angleOf(i) * Math.PI) / 180)).toFixed(2)}%; --y: ${(50 + R * Math.sin((angleOf(i) * Math.PI) / 180)).toFixed(2)}%;`}
                data-pop
                data-pop-delay={i * 70}
              >
                <span class="node__in">
                  {/* ⚠ A PLAIN img, NOT CmsImage. The node icon is 512px of
                      decoration inside a 44px circle: it needs no srcset, and
                      CmsImage drops the aria-hidden a decorative image must
                      carry — it also emits a bare `alt` where the original had
                      `alt=""`, which is the same to a browser and not the same
                      to a diff. */}
                  <img src={fileUrl(ab.icon)} alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
                  <span class="node__k">{ab.label}</span>
                </span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ═══ 04 · COLLABORATIVE LEARNING ════════════════════════════════════════
      One wide editorial frame that bleeds past the container, with the copy
      inset over it on glass — no columns, no cards. */}
  <section class="tp-four" aria-labelledby="tp-four-h">
    <figure class="tp-four__art" data-mask data-mask-from="left">
      <SmartImage
        file={four.image}
        alt={four.imageAlt}
       
        widths={[900, 1400, 1920]}
        sizes="100vw"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </figure>

    <div class="u-container tp-four__in">
      <div class="tp-four__plate" data-reveal>
        <p class="tp__n" aria-hidden="true">04</p>
        <p class="tp__k t-label">{four.kicker}</p>
        <h2 class="tp-four__h" id="tp-four-h" data-split>{four.heading}</h2>
        <RichLine class="tp__p" text={four.body[0]} />
      </div>
    </div>

    <img class="tp__f tp__f--shape" src={dShape.src} alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
  </section>

  {/* ═══ 05 · INNOVATIVE & TECHNOLOGY-ENABLED ═══════════════════════════════
      Layered: a frame, a soft glow, and the copy stepped off it. Kept on the
      PHILOSOPHY — the rooms and the equipment belong to Smart Classrooms. */}
  <section class="tp-five" aria-labelledby="tp-five-h">
    <span class="tp__wash tp__wash--b" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <div class="u-container tp-five__in">
      <div class="tp-five__copy">
        <p class="tp__n" aria-hidden="true">05</p>
        <p class="tp__k t-label" data-reveal>{five.kicker}</p>
        <h2 class="tp-five__h" id="tp-five-h" data-split>{five.heading}</h2>
        <RichLine class="tp__p" text={five.body[0]} reveal revealDelay={110} />
        <RichLine class="tp__p" text={five.body[1]} reveal revealDelay={180} />
      </div>

      <figure class="tp-five__art" data-parallax data-parallax-y="44">
        <SmartImage file={five.image} alt={five.imageAlt} widths={[480, 860]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 92vw, 40vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </figure>
    </div>

    <img class="tp__f tp__f--rocket" src={dRocket.src} alt="" aria-hidden="true" data-parallax data-parallax-y="-40" />
  </section>

  {/* ═══ CLOSING ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */}
  <section class="tp-end" aria-labelledby="tp-end-h">
    <figure class="tp-end__art">
      <SmartImage file={close.image} alt={close.imageAlt} widths={[900, 1400, 1920]} sizes="100vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </figure>
    <span class="tp-end__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <div class="u-container tp-end__in">
      <h2 class="tp-end__h" id="tp-end-h" data-split>
      {/* Any number of lines: the page puts the breaks in and sets the
          last one in italic. Three lines on one page, two on another. */}
      {close.headingLines.map((line, i) => (
        <>{i > 0 && <br />}{i === close.headingLines.length - 1 ? <em>{line}</em> : line}</>
      ))}
      </h2>
      <p class="tp-end__p" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="140">
        “{close.quote}”
      </p>
      <p class="tp-end__by" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="220">{close.quoteAuthor} · Principal</p>
    </div>

    <img class="tp__f tp__f--books" src={dBooks.src} alt="" aria-hidden="true" data-parallax data-parallax-y="-36" />
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .tp { position: relative; }
  .tp section { position: relative; isolation: isolate; overflow: hidden; }

  /* ═══ SHARED ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .tp__k { color: var(--sb-violet-dark); }
  .tp__k--onink { color: var(--sb-lime); }

  /* ⚠ THE NUMERAL IS ORNAMENT, SO IT IS aria-hidden AND NOT A HEADING. A screen
     reader announcing "zero one" before every section adds nothing a heading
     level does not already carry. */
  .tp__n {
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(44px, 6vw, 92px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.82;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    color: rgba(201, 60, 10, 0.16);
  }

  .tp__n--onink { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16); }

  :global(.tp__p) {
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin-top: var(--sb-4);
    font-size: clamp(15.5px, 1.15vw, 18px);
    line-height: 1.74;
    color: var(--sb-text-secondary);
  }

  :global(.tp__p em) { font-style: italic; color: var(--sb-charcoal); }
  :global(.tp__p strong) { font-weight: 700; color: var(--sb-charcoal); }
  :global(.tp__p--onink) { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82); }
  .tp__p--onink em,
  :global(.tp__p--onink strong) { color: #fff; }

  .tp-quote {
    margin: clamp(16px, 2vw, 22px) 0 0;
    padding-left: clamp(16px, 2vw, 22px);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--sb-violet);
  }

  .tp-quote p {
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(17px, 1.7vw, 24px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.42;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--sb-charcoal);
  }

  .tp-quote cite { display: block; margin-top: 9px; font-size: 13px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: var(--sb-violet-dark); }

  /* Backgrounds — drawn, never downloaded. */
  .tp__grid, .tp__dots, .tp__wash, .tp__orb { position: absolute; z-index: -1; pointer-events: none; }

  .tp__grid {
    inset: 0;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(to right, rgba(27, 21, 18, 0.045) 1px, transparent 1px),
      linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(27, 21, 18, 0.045) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 76px 76px;
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(78% 70% at 26% 22%, #000, transparent 76%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(78% 70% at 26% 22%, #000, transparent 76%);
  }

  .tp__dots {
    inset: 0;
    background-image: radial-gradient(currentColor 1.2px, transparent 1.2px);
    background-size: 26px 26px;
    color: rgba(201, 60, 10, 0.15);
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(70% 62% at 72% 40%, #000, transparent 74%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(70% 62% at 72% 40%, #000, transparent 74%);
  }

  .tp__dots--dark { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.13); }

  .tp__wash { border-radius: 50%; filter: blur(20px); }
  .tp__wash--a { top: -14%; right: -8%; width: min(46vw, 620px); aspect-ratio: 1; background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(201, 60, 10, 0.16) 0%, rgba(201, 60, 10, 0) 68%); }
  .tp__wash--b { bottom: -18%; left: -10%; width: min(40vw, 540px); aspect-ratio: 1; background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(255, 138, 92, 0.2) 0%, rgba(255, 138, 92, 0) 68%); }

  .tp__orb {
    top: 50%; left: 50%;
    width: min(86vw, 900px); aspect-ratio: 1;
    translate: -50% -50%;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(201, 60, 10, 0.46) 0%, rgba(255, 138, 92, 0.16) 42%, rgba(201, 60, 10, 0) 70%);
    filter: blur(30px);
    animation: tp-breathe 17s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  @keyframes tp-breathe { 0%,100% { transform: scale(1); opacity: .85 } 50% { transform: scale(1.1); opacity: 1 } }

  /* ⚠ DECORATION IS INERT AND SITS IN GUTTERS. Every float is aria-hidden with
     alt="", and pointer-events: none is load-bearing — these cross headings and
     images by design. Positions are anchored to an edge rather than to a
     percentage across the page, because a copy column grows as a share of the
     viewport while a 90px PNG does not: that is exactly how the philosophy page
     ended up with an ornament sitting on a heading at 1024 only. */
  .tp__f { position: absolute; z-index: 1; display: block; height: auto; pointer-events: none; user-select: none; }
  .tp__f--kite { top: 5%; right: 4%; width: clamp(52px, 6.5vw, 100px); animation: tp-bob 13s ease-in-out infinite; }
  .tp__f--stars { top: 8%; right: 22%; width: clamp(30px, 3.6vw, 56px); opacity: .8; }
  .tp__f--bulb { top: 4%; right: 4%; width: clamp(44px, 5.2vw, 84px); animation: tp-bob 15s ease-in-out infinite; }
  /* ⚠ RIGHT, NOT LEFT. On the left it landed square on §05's oversized "05" —
     the numeral opens the copy column, and the copy column is the left half at
     900+. Measured, not guessed. */
  .tp__f--rocket { top: 4%; right: 3%; width: clamp(50px, 6vw, 96px); animation: tp-bob 14s ease-in-out infinite; }
  .tp__f--star { top: 6%; right: 5%; width: clamp(28px, 3.2vw, 50px); animation: tp-spin 30s linear infinite; }
  .tp__f--shape { bottom: 4%; left: 2%; width: clamp(56px, 7vw, 118px); opacity: .5; }
  .tp__f--books { top: 6%; right: 4%; width: clamp(48px, 6vw, 92px); }

  @keyframes tp-bob { 0%,100% { transform: translate3d(0,0,0) } 50% { transform: translate3d(0,-15px,0) } }
  @keyframes tp-spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg) } }

  /* ═══ 01 ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .tp-one { padding-block: clamp(52px, 8vw, 108px); background: var(--sb-ivory); }
  .tp-one__in { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr); gap: clamp(30px, 4.6vw, 66px); align-items: center; }

  .tp-one__h {
    margin-top: var(--sb-3);
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.8vw, 62px);
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -.04em;
    color: var(--sb-charcoal); text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .tp-one__h em { font-style: normal; color: var(--sb-violet); }

  .tp-one__art { margin: 0; overflow: hidden; border-radius: var(--sb-r-3); box-shadow: 0 40px 80px -46px rgba(27,21,18,.6); }
  .tp-one__art :global(img) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }

  /* ═══ 02 ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .tp-two { padding-block: clamp(52px, 8vw, 108px); background: var(--sb-sand); }
  .tp-two__in { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr); gap: clamp(34px, 5vw, 70px); align-items: center; }

  .tp-two__stage { position: relative; padding-bottom: clamp(40px, 8vw, 90px); }

  .tp-two__a, .tp-two__b { margin: 0; overflow: hidden; border-radius: var(--sb-r-3); box-shadow: 0 34px 70px -42px rgba(27,21,18,.6); }
  .tp-two__a :global(img), .tp-two__b :global(img) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }

  .tp-two__b { position: absolute; right: 0; bottom: 0; width: 56%; border: 6px solid var(--sb-sand); }

  .tp-two__link { position: absolute; inset: 34% 8% 12% 12%; width: auto; height: auto; color: var(--sb-violet); opacity: .5; }

  .tp-two__h {
    margin-top: var(--sb-3);
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 52px);
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -.038em;
    color: var(--sb-charcoal); text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* ═══ 03 ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  /* Asymmetric on purpose: the head needs far less room above it than the
     constellation needs below, and 122px of empty ink above the "03" was reading
     as a gap rather than as breathing room. */
  .tp-three { padding: clamp(26px, 3.4vw, 52px) 0 clamp(60px, 9vw, 122px); background: var(--sb-violet-ink); }
  .tp-three__in { position: relative; z-index: 1; }

  /* Full container width, not 56ch. At the old measure the heading broke across
     two lines and the standfirst ran to four, so the widest section on the page
     was introduced by the narrowest column on it. */
  .tp-three__head { max-width: none; margin-inline: auto; text-align: center; }

  /* ⚠ SCOPED, NOT A CHANGE TO .tp__p. That rule is a 52ch column with no auto
     margin, which is exactly right for the left-aligned movements that share it.
     Inside 03's now-full-width centred head it kept hugging the left edge, so the
     standfirst sat in the left half of the section under a centred heading. */
  .tp-three__head .tp__p { max-width: 92ch; margin-inline: auto; }

  .tp-three__h {
    margin-top: var(--sb-3);
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4.4vw, 58px);
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -.042em;
    color: #fff; text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* The constellation. A square stage; nodes are placed by angle on a CSS
     custom property, so adding an ability is one array entry. */
  .tp-const {
    position: relative;
    width: min(100%, 620px);
    margin: clamp(38px, 5vw, 66px) auto 0;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
  }

  .tp-const__rings { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; color: rgba(255,255,255,.22); }

  .tp-const__core {
    position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%;
    width: 32%; aspect-ratio: 1;
    translate: -50% -50%;
    overflow: hidden; border-radius: 50%;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px rgba(255,255,255,.1), 0 30px 60px -28px rgba(0,0,0,.7);
  }

  /* ⚠ THE <picture> HAS TO BE STRETCHED, NOT JUST THE <img>. `astro:assets`
     emits <picture><img></picture>, and <picture> is an INLINE box: it takes its
     intrinsic height, so the img's `height: 100%` resolved against that instead
     of against the circle. The photo rendered as a rectangle sitting inside a
     visible circular outline. Pinning the picture to the frame's inset is what
     makes the round crop real. */
  .tp-const__core :global(picture) { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: block; }

  /* 42%, not 50% — the frame's true centre is the thread basket, and lifting the
     crop brings two faces into a circle this small. */
  .tp-const__core :global(img) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 42%; }

  .tp-const__set { position: absolute; inset: 0; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }

  /* Placed by percentage — see the note on `R` in the frontmatter for why this
     is not a rotate→translate transform. */
  .node {
    position: absolute;
    top: var(--y);
    left: var(--x);
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
  }

  .node__in {
    display: grid; place-items: center; gap: 6px;
    width: clamp(76px, 12vw, 108px);
    padding: 10px 6px;
    /* The only transform needed now: centre the box on its point. */
    translate: -50% -50%;
    border-radius: var(--sb-r-2);
    /* A LIGHT plate on a near-black section, which is the opposite of the first
       build. The tiles were rgba(255,255,255,.08) and the ornament PNGs — cap,
       bulb, saturn, brush — are dark artwork drawn for light ground, so four of
       the seven nodes were all but invisible in the render. Nothing about the
       icons changed; the plate under them did. */
    background: rgba(251, 247, 244, .95);
    box-shadow: 0 18px 34px -22px rgba(0,0,0,.9), inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(28,14,8,.08);
  }

  /* A FIXED SLOT, not `height: auto`. The ornament PNGs have wildly different
     intrinsic ratios — the pencil is tall, the brush is wide — so an auto height
     made every tile a different height and the labels sat at seven different
     baselines. Squaring the slot and letting `contain` letterbox inside it lines
     the labels up without cropping any artwork. */
  .node__in img {
    display: block;
    width: clamp(28px, 3.6vw, 40px);
    height: clamp(28px, 3.6vw, 40px);
    object-fit: contain;
  }
  .node__k { font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--sb-violet-ink); }

  /* ═══ 04 ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .tp-four { padding-block: clamp(56px, 9vw, 120px); background: var(--sb-charcoal); }

  .tp-four__art { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -2; margin: 0; }
  .tp-four__art :global(picture) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  .tp-four__art :global(img) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }

  .tp-four__in { position: relative; z-index: 1; }

  /* ⚠ THE PLATE CARRIES ITS OWN GROUND. White copy over an unmodified
     photograph is only safe if the plate alone can hold it — this frame is a
     sunlit ground, so the plate is 0.82 rather than a light tint. */
  .tp-four__plate {
    max-width: 640px;
    padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px);
    border-radius: var(--sb-r-3);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.9) inset, 0 40px 80px -40px rgba(0,0,0,.7);
    backdrop-filter: blur(18px) saturate(150%);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(18px) saturate(150%);
  }

  @supports not ((backdrop-filter: blur(2px)) or (-webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(2px))) {
    .tp-four__plate { background: #fff; }
  }

  .tp-four__h {
    margin-top: var(--sb-3);
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.8vw, 48px);
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -.036em;
    color: var(--sb-charcoal);
  }

  /* ═══ 05 ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .tp-five { padding-block: clamp(52px, 8vw, 108px); background: var(--sb-ivory); }
  .tp-five__in { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr); gap: clamp(30px, 4.6vw, 66px); align-items: center; }

  .tp-five__h {
    margin-top: var(--sb-3);
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 52px);
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -.038em;
    color: var(--sb-charcoal); text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .tp-five__art { margin: 0; overflow: hidden; border-radius: var(--sb-r-3); box-shadow: 0 36px 74px -44px rgba(27,21,18,.6); }
  .tp-five__art :global(img) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }

  /* ═══ 06 ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

  /* ═══ CLOSING ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .tp-end { padding-block: clamp(76px, 12vw, 156px); background: var(--sb-violet-ink); }

  .tp-end__art { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -2; margin: 0; }
  .tp-end__art :global(picture) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  .tp-end__art :global(img) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }

  .tp-end__scrim {
    position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -1;
    background:
      radial-gradient(70% 60% at 30% 40%, rgba(28,14,8,.6) 0%, rgba(28,14,8,0) 70%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(28,14,8,.72) 0%, rgba(28,14,8,.56) 42%, rgba(28,14,8,.86) 100%);
  }

  .tp-end__in { position: relative; z-index: 1; text-align: center; }

  .tp-end__h {
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(32px, 5.4vw, 76px);
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -.044em;
    color: #fff; text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .tp-end__h em { font-style: normal; color: var(--sb-lime); }

  .tp-end__p {
    max-width: 48ch;
    margin: clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 28px) auto 0;
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(17px, 1.6vw, 23px);
    font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.5;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.92);
  }

  .tp-end__by { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sb-lime); }

  /* ═══ LAYOUT ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     ⚠ MOBILE IS RE-COMPOSED, NOT STACKED. The diagonal pair in §02 comes out of
     its overlap and the connector goes with it — a dashed line between two
     frames that are no longer diagonal is a line to nowhere. The constellation
     keeps its geometry because it is angular rather than columnar, but its
     radius and node size shrink together so the ring never collides with the
     core. */
  /* ═══ THE CONSTELLATION TURNS ═══════════════════════════════════
     ⚠⚠ THE SET ROTATES AND EACH PLATE COUNTER-ROTATES BY THE SAME AMOUNT, which
     is the only way the nodes can travel a circle while their labels stay
     upright. Both use the same duration and linear timing, or the two stop
     cancelling and the words wobble.

     ⚠ THE rotate PROPERTY, NOT transform. .node__in already carries
     translate: -50% -50% to centre itself on its point; animating transform
     would overwrite that and every plate would jump down-right by half its own
     size. The independent transform properties compose instead of colliding.

     ⚠ EVERY WIDTH, now that the ring survives on phones too. It was scoped to
     >=701px when the mobile layout was a flat grid, where rotating would have
     sent the tiles round the page.

     ⚠ SLOW. 90s for a full turn is about 4° a second: the eye reads it as alive
     rather than as something spinning. The dashed ring runs the other way at 60s
     so the two motions are distinguishable. */
  @media (min-width: 0px) {
    .tp-const__set { animation: tp-orbit 90s linear infinite; }
    .node__in { animation: tp-orbit-counter 90s linear infinite; }
    .tp-const__dash {
      transform-box: fill-box;
      transform-origin: center;
      animation: tp-orbit-counter 60s linear infinite;
    }

    /* Pointing at it stops the drift, so a reader can look at one node without
       it walking away from the cursor. */
    .tp-const:hover .tp-const__set,
    .tp-const:hover .node__in,
    .tp-const:focus-within .tp-const__set,
    .tp-const:focus-within .node__in { animation-play-state: paused; }
  }

  @keyframes tp-orbit {
    from { rotate: 0deg; }
    to { rotate: 360deg; }
  }
  @keyframes tp-orbit-counter {
    from { rotate: 0deg; }
    to { rotate: -360deg; }
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .tp-one__in { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1.02fr) minmax(0,.98fr); }
    .tp-two__in { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,.95fr) minmax(0,1.05fr); }
    .tp-five__in { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1.05fr) minmax(0,.95fr); }
  }

  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .tp-two__b { position: static; width: 100%; margin-top: clamp(14px, 2.4vw, 20px); border-width: 0; }
    .tp-two__link { display: none; }
    .tp-two__stage { padding-bottom: 0; }
    /* Below the two-column breakpoints the copy fills the width, so there is no
       gutter left for corner ornament to sit in without landing on it. */
    .tp__f--stars,
    .tp__f--rocket { display: none; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    /* ⚠⚠ THE RING IS KEPT ON PHONES NOW. It used to unwind here into a chip
       grid — same content, different shape — and the section then looked like a
       different design on a phone than on a laptop. It turns out the ring did
       not need abandoning: --x/--y are PERCENTAGES of the stage, so the geometry
       already scales on its own. The only thing that did not scale was the plate,
       which is sized in px.

       ⚠ THE PLATES OVERHANG THE CONTAINER GUTTER, AND THAT IS FINE. What must
       not be exceeded is the VIEWPORT, not the 24px container padding — the
       section ground is full-bleed, so a plate reaching into the gutter still
       sits on the same dark field. At 390px the outermost edge lands at 175px
       from centre against a 195px half-viewport; at 320px, 147px against 160px.

       ⚠ CHECKED FOR THE TWO WAYS A SMALL RING BREAKS: adjacent plates colliding
       (centres are 123px apart at 390px, plates are 74px — 49px of air) and
       plates swallowing the centre portrait (inner edge 100px out, core radius
       55px). An earlier build hid the seventh node to buy room, which quietly
       deleted an intelligence from the one section arguing there is more than
       one. Nothing is hidden here. */
    .node__in {
      width: clamp(68px, 19vw, 108px);
      padding: 8px 5px;
      gap: 4px;
    }
    .node__in img { width: 26px; height: 26px; }
    /* 10.5px, not the desktop 11.5 — “Invention” is the longest label and has to
       clear the narrower plate on one line. Letter-spacing goes too; at this size
       it buys nothing and costs 3px. */
    .node__k { font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0; }

    .tp__f--rocket, .tp__f--shape { display: none; }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .tp__f, .tp__orb { animation: none; }
    /* The constellation is still readable standing still — it just stops. */
    .tp-const__set, .node__in, .tp-const__dash { animation: none; }
  }
</style>
